  "body": {
    "id": "prop:single-donor-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "When \\(J=1\\), \\(A_{\\mathrm{PT}}=0\\), so profiling the sole treated-versus-donor equality leaves no PT observed-data normal and the PT observed-law tangent space is unrestricted. At every intersection law the full-rank SC observed model is therefore locally nested in the PT observed model, \\(\\mathcal I_{\\mathrm{PT}}(P_0)\\subseteq\\mathcal I_{\\mathrm{SC}}(P_0)\\), \\(\\phi_U=\\phi_{\\mathrm{PT}}\\), and \\(V_U=V_{\\mathrm{PT}}\\). With \\(T=2\\), this PT gradient equals the panel-DiD ATT efficient influence function in SantAnnaZhao2020, Proposition 1.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "J",
      "P0",
      "Ib",
      "phiU",
      "phib",
      "VU",
      "Vb",
      "T",
